I was, i'm afraid, picking on the (very common) typo of 'diety' for
'deity'. While 'deities' are divine beings, 'dieties' isn't an english
word; a good approximation would be 'dietary entities'.

The wrong spelling is, alas, so widely considered correct[1] that it's
incredibly difficult to make fun of it without engaging in long-winded
explanations.

[1] 'dieties' gets over two hundred thousand google hits, and most of
these do indeed talk about deities, not dieties (whatever the latter
may be). It's a bit of a consolation that 'deities' gets over 10
million hits.

